    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.cmdline\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12.x\n\n### Description\n\nTyping `echo &` into the command line throws `E112: option name missing: &` (pictured below).\n\n### Reproduction\n\nUsing this config:\n\n```lua\nvim.pack.add({\n\t\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim\",\n})\nrequire(\"mini.cmdline\").setup()\n```\n\nsimply open neovim, go to the command line with `:`, and type `echo &`. The error is thrown.\n\n<img width=\"379\" height=\"117\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ac52dbe0-a73d-4854-a6a4-3bce0cc6dfb1\" />",
