        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Not sure how helpful this is, but this is also an issue with kickstart.nvim (and it doesn't use mini.cmdline):\n\n```sh\ngit clone https://github.com/nvim-lua/kickstart.nvim.git ~/.config/kickstart.nvim\nNVIM_APPNAME=kickstart.nvim nvim\n```\n(and, it seems to be an issue with any syntax errors during typing. For instance `:echo \"`)\n\n<img width=\"351\" height=\"400\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/531a4e2a-e213-448f-b724-e85c46291310\" />\n\nmini.nvim configuration is here:\n\nhttps://github.com/nvim-lua/kickstart.nvim/blob/d3168308d47e60d772f592ccc132f27c72437cd3/init.lua#L834-L868\n\nAlthough, unfortunately, I could not reproduce with a similar minimal `repro.lua`:\n\n```lua\nvim.pack.add({\n\t\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim\",\n})\n\nrequire(\"mini.ai\").setup({ n_lines = 500 })\n\nrequire(\"mini.surround\").setup()\n\nlocal statusline = require(\"mini.statusline\")\nstatusline.setup({ use_icons = vim.g.have_nerd_font })\nstatusline.section_location = function()\n\treturn \"%2l:%-2v\"\nend\n```",
