        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "After investigating, this is most certainly not a 'mini.cmdline' issue. The problem is that `vim.api.nvim_parse_cmd('echo &', {})` shows the error here, although arguably it should not *and* using `pcall()` (i.e. to suppress any error) does not work here. This happens even on `nvim --clean`, both on 0.12.0 and latest `master`.\n\nI'll report the issue upstream at least tomorrow (if anybody has time and aspiration, you can create it sooner).\n\nIn the meantime, if this bothers too much, disabling `autopeek` (`config.autopeek.enable = false`) seems to be the smallest scope needed to make it not error. Unfortunately, there doesn't seem to be any other way for 'mini.cmdline' to handle this other than make sure that it is fixed upstream and released in 0.12.1.",
